WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:04.080
So listen, this, this next story gives me
no pleasure to tell you this, but I do a political

00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:09.809
show and when I have a personal experience
that's relevant to the 2020 democratic primary,

00:00:09.809 --> 00:00:12.260
that is an important topic on this program.

00:00:12.260 --> 00:00:13.361
I have to tell you about it.

00:00:13.361 --> 00:00:15.370
It would be really weird for me not to talk
about this.

00:00:15.370 --> 00:00:19.560
Now, as many of you know, I'm voting for Bernie
Sanders in the Massachusetts primary on March

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:23.580
3rd, I would vote for any of the democratic
candidates over Donald Trump and I will support

00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:24.640
the eventual nominee.

00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:25.640
Good.

00:00:25.640 --> 00:00:26.640
Uh, yeah.

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:27.640
Good.

00:00:27.640 --> 00:00:28.640
Okay.

00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:33.320
So, so far I've been canvassed by two campaigns
here in Massachusetts.

00:00:33.320 --> 00:00:39.550
Two weeks ago a Bloomberg canvasser volunteer
came to my door and talk to me about Michael

00:00:39.550 --> 00:00:40.550
Bloomberg.

00:00:40.550 --> 00:00:46.590
Um, and this week, the Bernie Sanders campaign,
it came to my door to Bernie Sanders.

00:00:46.590 --> 00:00:47.980
They were volunteers.

00:00:47.980 --> 00:00:48.980
This was not paid.

00:00:48.980 --> 00:00:49.989
Staff came to my door.

00:00:49.989 --> 00:00:56.060
Uh, I didn't immediately tell them who I was
voting for and they very quickly, instead

00:00:56.060 --> 00:01:02.100
of talking up Bernie about his policies, they
immediately started attacking Elizabeth Warren

00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:03.550
to my face.

00:01:03.550 --> 00:01:05.590
And I think this is a terrible strategy.

00:01:05.590 --> 00:01:09.320
If I were Bernie Sanders, I wouldn't want
my canvassers doing this.

00:01:09.320 --> 00:01:10.929
And by the way, I'm sure Bernie does it.

00:01:10.929 --> 00:01:16.649
I mean clearly these were folks who were not
following, you know, patent max a told, hold

00:01:16.649 --> 00:01:21.340
us on the bonus show last week that they went
up to New Hampshire to canvas for Bernie ahead

00:01:21.340 --> 00:01:26.149
of the New Hampshire primary and they had
an app and the app outlines how to handle

00:01:26.149 --> 00:01:29.450
different types of objections a and nowhere
in there.

00:01:29.450 --> 00:01:31.529
Was there anything about attacking other candidates?

00:01:31.529 --> 00:01:36.840
So to be very clear, these were obviously
not individuals acting on the direction from

00:01:36.840 --> 00:01:42.939
the Bernie Sanders campaign, but it should
be made super clear I think to everybody who

00:01:42.939 --> 00:01:49.170
is volunteering to canvas for Bernie or whoever
do not bad mouth other candidates don't do

00:01:49.170 --> 00:01:54.509
it because it makes you look bad and also
don't do it because if the primary thing in

00:01:54.509 --> 00:02:00.659
the end is to remove Donald Trump, we don't
want to campaign for our candidate in a way

00:02:00.659 --> 00:02:05.789
that could potentially hurt the eventual nominee
in the future if it is to be someone else

00:02:05.789 --> 00:02:10.780
and they they the people who came to my door,
to the Bernie supporters, the canvassers were

00:02:10.780 --> 00:02:16.010
saying things like, we support Bernie because
Elizabeth Warren doesn't really care about

00:02:16.010 --> 00:02:18.310
working people like Bernie does.

00:02:18.310 --> 00:02:20.250
They said that on healthcare.

00:02:20.250 --> 00:02:27.010
Elizabeth Warren doesn't even care about giving
everyone health care right away and I think

00:02:27.010 --> 00:02:30.450
the spontaneous attacks on Warren are bad.

00:02:30.450 --> 00:02:34.850
Maybe here in Massachusetts we're seeing some
of it because the last poll we have is from

00:02:34.850 --> 00:02:38.730
October, but at the time Warren was the presumptive
front runner here.

00:02:38.730 --> 00:02:42.060
Although we haven't had a poll in months,
and I don't know who's actually winning.

00:02:42.060 --> 00:02:47.760
Uh, and I don't even think that using the
word, I don't think Warren wants to give everyone

00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:48.760
healthcare.

00:02:48.760 --> 00:02:51.440
I don't even think that's the right language
in my mind.

00:02:51.440 --> 00:02:57.980
I would be talking about Bernie wants to ensure
everybody receives the healthcare they need,

00:02:57.980 --> 00:03:01.600
which to me sounds better than using this
language of giving everyone healthcare.

00:03:01.600 --> 00:03:05.750
So again, these were volunteer canvassers.

00:03:05.750 --> 00:03:11.220
Um, they are, you know, based on what Pat
told us, they get a 30 minute training of

00:03:11.220 --> 00:03:14.590
some kind before going out there and doing
their thing.

00:03:14.590 --> 00:03:18.090
Um, clearly these were folks who I give them
the benefit of the doubt.

00:03:18.090 --> 00:03:19.600
I assume they have the best intentions.

00:03:19.600 --> 00:03:22.600
They're campaigning for the person they think
is best for the country, and they're doing

00:03:22.600 --> 00:03:25.710
it vigorously and they are trying to do it
in the way that they believe would be most

00:03:25.710 --> 00:03:27.390
persuasive but persuasive.

00:03:27.390 --> 00:03:32.160
But the point is, if Bernie is the nominee,
we don't gain anything.

00:03:32.160 --> 00:03:36.650
By going around and attacking Elizabeth Warren
to people you've just met, who you haven't

00:03:36.650 --> 00:03:38.940
even revealed yet how they plan to vote.

00:03:38.940 --> 00:03:44.710
Had I been a Warren support supporter, am
I going to be convinced to vote Bernie because

00:03:44.710 --> 00:03:51.410
two canvassers showed up at my house and trashed
the person that may be I'm considering supporting.

00:03:51.410 --> 00:03:52.410
I don't think so.

00:03:52.410 --> 00:03:55.280
I'm not going to say, you know, I didn't think
about that about it that way.

00:03:55.280 --> 00:03:57.520
Warren doesn't care about working people.

00:03:57.520 --> 00:03:59.640
I'm going to switch my vote to Bernie.

00:03:59.640 --> 00:04:01.190
I'm not blaming Bernie.

00:04:01.190 --> 00:04:02.880
These aren't paid campaign staff.

00:04:02.880 --> 00:04:06.120
These were volunteers, but it's not good in
general.

00:04:06.120 --> 00:04:09.319
You don't want to do canvassing where you
show up and attack other candidates, either

00:04:09.319 --> 00:04:14.130
point out objective policy, policy, things
that you believe another candidate has done

00:04:14.130 --> 00:04:15.130
wrong.

00:04:15.130 --> 00:04:17.150
Say Elizabeth Warren signed this and Bernie
was against it.

00:04:17.150 --> 00:04:18.150
Oh, okay.

00:04:18.150 --> 00:04:19.639
Well that, that's information that's useful.

00:04:19.639 --> 00:04:25.129
But in reality, just talk about why the person
you support is the best person and why I should

00:04:25.129 --> 00:04:26.129
vote for them.

00:04:26.129 --> 00:04:31.729
And there's, you know, a lot of really bogus,
uh, Bernie bro was mean on Twitter stuff floating

00:04:31.729 --> 00:04:33.520
around the internet.

00:04:33.520 --> 00:04:35.080
That's not what this is.

00:04:35.080 --> 00:04:40.759
That is actually a coordinated campaign to
go after Bernie supporters as a proxy to attacking

00:04:40.759 --> 00:04:41.759
Bernie.

00:04:41.759 --> 00:04:46.580
I'm talking merely about campaign strategy
and I think that attacking other candidates

00:04:46.580 --> 00:04:49.580
at people's doors is bad strategy.

00:04:49.580 --> 00:04:56.419
It's likely that these individuals, uh, were,
were a little, um, overexuberant and they

00:04:56.419 --> 00:04:58.139
went in a direction that didn't make sense.

00:04:58.139 --> 00:05:02.199
And in fact, Pat said a lot of what he was
doing when he canvassed for Bernie in New

00:05:02.199 --> 00:05:07.990
Hampshire was ascertaining if the person planned
to vote for Bernie Sanders and, uh, saying,

00:05:07.990 --> 00:05:10.759
you know, consider Bernie in a more friendly
way.

00:05:10.759 --> 00:05:11.759
Let me know what you think of this.

00:05:11.759 --> 00:05:16.919
Let me know if anybody has canvas you and
whether you experienced something similar,

00:05:16.919 --> 00:05:20.270
different from Bernie canvassers or other
canvassers.

00:05:20.270 --> 00:05:25.681
Again, I've only been approached by Bloomberg
supporters, Bloomberg campaign people, and

00:05:25.681 --> 00:05:26.681
Bernie campaign people.

00:05:26.681 --> 00:05:26.819
At this point in time

